              <b>6 shifts</b> in total, and 8 comparisons.</li>
            <li>Line 5. It compares with <code>arr[i]</code>, so it finds the last value smaller than <code>arr[i]</code>, not the smallest. It should be <code>if (arr[j] &lt; arr[minIndex])</code>.</li>
            <li>(a) <b>Insertion sort</b> (or bubble sort): it must be stable, and selection sort is not. (b) <b>Insertion sort</b>: the list is almost sorted, so each late enrollee is shifted into place with little work. (c) <b>Selection sort</b>: only n - 1 swaps.</li>
